  "talk": [
    { "text": "Every unwholesome moment carries the same four: " },
    { "term": "moha", "surface": "moha" },
    { "text": " not seeing clearly, " },
    { "term": "ahirika", "surface": "ahirika" },
    { "text": " and " },
    { "term": "anottappa", "surface": "anottappa" },
    { "text": " with no brake inside or out, and " },
    { "term": "uddhacca", "surface": "uddhacca" },
    { "text": " shaking it all. Then the mind takes a direction. Toward the object: " },
    { "term": "lobha", "surface": "lobha" },
    { "text": " grasps, " },
    { "term": "ditthi", "surface": "diṭṭhi" },
    { "text": " builds a story about it, " },
    { "term": "mana", "surface": "māna" },
    { "text": " measures me against you. Against the object: " },
    { "term": "dosa", "surface": "dosa" },
    { "text": " strikes, " },
    { "term": "issa", "surface": "issā" },
    { "text": " resents what you have, " },
    { "term": "macchariya", "surface": "macchariya" },
    { "text": " hides what I have, " },
    { "term": "kukkucca", "surface": "kukkucca" },
    { "text": " picks at what I did. Or the mind simply sinks — " },
    { "term": "thina", "surface": "thīna" },
    { "text": " and " },
    { "term": "middha", "surface": "middha" },
    { "text": " — or wobbles in " },
    { "term": "vicikiccha", "surface": "vicikicchā" },
    { "text": ". Fourteen names for weather already familiar from the hindrances." }
  ],
  "suttaRec": {
    "title": "Akusalamūla — Unwholesome Roots",
    "ref": "an3.69",
    "url": "https://suttacentral.net/an3.69",
    "blurb": "Greed, hatred, and delusion as the three roots, each traced from the factor to the act to the fruit — and their wholesome opposites.",
    "minutes": 8
  }
}
